---
/**
 * /about — who publishes this, and under what boundaries.
 *
 * Deliberately short and free of personal detail. The handle is the identity;
 * there is nothing here that a real name could be recovered from.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';

import '../styles/prose.css';

const DESCRIPTION =
  'Detection engineering, KQL, and threat hunting notes, published under the handle leftanti.';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={DESCRIPTION}>
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1 class="page-head__title">About</h1>
    <p class="page-head__sub"><span aria-hidden="true">//</span> the handle, the scope, the boundaries</p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>The handle</h2>

    <p>
      A <code>leftanti</code> join returns the rows on the left that have no match on the
      right — what is there when you subtract everything accounted for. That is most of
      detection work: not finding the thing that matches, but noticing what is left once
      everything explainable has been removed.
    </p>

    <p>
      The site mark draws it literally. Two overlapping circles, the left one filled with
      the intersection cut away, the right one outlined and empty.
    </p>

    <h2>The scope</h2>

    <p>
      Notes on detection engineering, KQL, and threat hunting, mostly against Microsoft
      Sentinel and Defender. Queries are written to be copied, adapted, and tuned against
      your own data — not deployed as-is. Every threshold here is a starting point, and
      every one of them is wrong for somebody's tenant.
    </p>

    <p>
      There is no comments section, no newsletter, and no tracking. The site makes no
      requests to anything other than its own origin: no fonts from a CDN, no analytics,
      no embeds.
    </p>

    <h2>The boundaries</h2>

    <p>
      All content is my own, published in a personal capacity. Everything here is built
      from scratch on my own time and infrastructure — nothing derives from any employer's
      or client's environment.
    </p>

    <p>
      Table names, techniques, and thresholds in examples are generic or invented. Where a
      query references a watchlist or a lookup, that is an illustration of a pattern rather
      than a description of a real one.
    </p>

    {
      /* Rendered only for contact routes that actually exist. With neither set
         the whole section is omitted rather than showing a dead link — see
         src/config/site.ts. */
      (SITE.github || SITE.email) && (
        <Fragment>
          <h2>Contact</h2>

          <ul>
            {SITE.email && (
              <li>
                <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
              </li>
            )}
            {SITE.github && (
              <li>
                <a href={SITE.github} rel="me noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
                  {SITE.github.replace('https://', '')}
                </a>
              </li>
            )}
          </ul>

          <p>
            Corrections are welcome, particularly on the tuning notes — those are the parts
            most likely to be wrong outside the environment they were written against.
          </p>
        </Fragment>
      )
    }
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head {
    margin-block-end: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .page-head__title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-h2);
    font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-normal);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .page-head__sub {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-meta);
    line-height: var(--lh-snug);
    color: var(--text-comment);
  }
</style>
